  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "onZtvsN7gOwh6F9ZGetr5jCHr2E=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:37:55.101Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Three hooks read the selected document, and they differ only in how they handle absence.\n\n`useSelectedDocument()` resolves the selected node id, calls `useDocumentById`, and throws if nothing came back:\n\n```ts\nconst [document, dispatch] = useDocumentById(selectedDocumentId);\nif (!document) throw new NoSelectedDocumentError();\nreturn [document, dispatch] as const;\n```\n\nThe error message is self-documenting: *\"There is no selected document. Did you mean to call 'useSelectedDocumentSafe' instead?\"* Because it throws, `document` is non-nullable in the returned tuple \u2014 that is the whole point of the variant, and it means an `if (!document)` guard after the call is dead code.\n\n`useSelectedDocumentSafe()` is the same lookup with the throw removed \u2014 it is literally `return useDocumentById(selectedDocumentId)` \u2014 so it yields `[PHDocument | undefined, dispatch]`. Reach for it whenever \"no document selected\" is a state your component should render, not an invariant violation. Note that `undefined` is also what you get while a real document is still loading, so the Safe variant cannot distinguish \"nothing selected\" from \"not here yet\".\n\n`useSelectedDocumentOfType(documentType)` layers a type check on top. It throws `NoSelectedDocumentError` when no document is selected and `DocumentTypeMismatchError` when the selected document is a different type. It has one quirk: passing a `null`/`undefined` `documentType` returns an empty array (`never[]`) rather than throwing, so the hook can be called conditionally on a type that is not known yet.\n\n**Documentation caveat:** the React Hooks reference page attaches a copy-pasted *\"Throws: NoSelectedDocumentError\"* block to the `useSelectedDocumentSafe` section, and its example calls the non-Safe hook. That contradicts both the same section's own prose and the source. The Safe variant does not throw.\n\n_Source: packages/reactor-browser/src/hooks/selected-document.ts and src/errors.ts, cross-checked against apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/05-EditorsUI/01-ReactHooks.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:37:54.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:37:55.101Z"
    }
  },
